Windows reduce-motion and reduce-transparency settings, for 0039's platform hook.

What (needs 0039):
- gpui_windows: `accessibility_display.rs` (new, pure): `SPI_GETCLIENTAREAANIMATION` off (Settings > Accessibility >
  Visual effects > Animation effects) reduces motion; `EnableTransparency` = 0 under
  `HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Themes\Personalize` (Personalization > Colors > Transparency
  effects) reduces transparency; an unreadable or missing value reduces neither. platform.rs reads both at startup
  (windows-registry, already a dependency) and again on `WM_SETTINGCHANGE`, which the platform's hidden top-level
  window receives; it posts itself `WM_GPUI_ACCESSIBILITY_DISPLAY_CHANGED` (`WM_USER + 11`) first, as for display
  changes, and calls the app back only when the settings moved. Table test runs on the host through
  scripts/patch-test.sh's `windows-pure` crate.

Why: 0039 gives GPUI a platform hook for the OS's reduce-motion and reduce-transparency settings; Windows reported
neither. The platform's message handling is private to gpui_windows.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

